    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d223">

                <pb facs="0216" n="894" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg894"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Pike.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 103.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-06-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 8, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 20th ultimo (No. 87)
                    relative to the question of the Scheldt tolls, to the Polish insurrection, and
                    to the impression produced by General Banks’s movements, has been received and
                    perused with much interest.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Pike</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c</hi>., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
